I had hoped to have more in this particular update, but I got pulled
away by pesky RealLife(tm) for a large portion of the weekend, so instead 
it's just going to be what you see here.  More coming soon.

As always, Windows binaries will show up this evening sometime.  At some
point I hope to actually get tiles in place for everything; I realize at
this point it actually won't even compile properly as a tiled version,
but drawing tiles _also_ takes time.  :)

11/11: save compatibility broken with this change

* Bug fix: bags of tricks now blow up bags of holding again; other bags 
  no longer do
* New item: small sacks.  Probability taken from other tool types, so 
  they should overall increase the chances of getting a "useful bag" type 
  randomly in the dungeon.
* New mechanic: sacks, oilskin sacks, and large boxes have a maximum capacity, 
  and most "big" things don't fit in small sacks
  -- Other containers also have a max capacity, but it should be sufficiently 
  difficult to reach as to not impact play.
* New shields added (placeholders given non-zero random generation chance now)
* Two new helms added to the mix and a new helmet type effect
* Two new pairs of gloves added to the mix
* Details for the new items here: http://sporkhack.com/newtoys.html

11/5:

* Uruk-hai shields now also get orcish racial bonus (previously only red-eyed 
  shields did)

